[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940106799","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3940106799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3940106799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q2UIv","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T04:15:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T10:05:47Z","body":"### Some other notes\r\n* I feel pretty confident there's a few more memory improvements that could be implemented in how the Batcher processes Multirect commands, some of the C++ nuances are still tricky for me\r\n* There could also be better batching between Multirect & Rect commands, there's probably a few cases where they can be processed in the same batch\r\n* The 'frontend' usage of Multirect is just the bare minimum to prove it works. There are probably better ways to integrate it into the TextServer, Labels, and TileMapLayers, and it is not yet used by RichTextLabels","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940106799/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940626015","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3940626015","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3940626015,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q4S5f","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T10:03:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T10:03:58Z","body":"Pushed a TileMap implementation - went with a straightforward implementation of having TileMapLayer set up a 'multirect' for each Dirty Quadrant processed in _rendering_update. Edit top-level comment with Performance info.\r\n\r\nThere's a possibility that some more complicated tiles aren't handled correctly by this yet, but I'd have to test further. I also feel confident there could be further optimization to how TileMapLayers actually make use of MultiRects.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940626015/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3943696824","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3943696824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3943696824,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rEAm4","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T09:47:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:47:49Z","body":"Pushed a few additions to the Multirect API, but no 'behavior' changes. I was drafting a version of this where MultiRect is better integrated into Labels/TextServer, but it's pretty difficult to integrate that behavior without more invasive changes to both, and I think it merits a separate discussion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3943696824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3963566115","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3963566115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3963566115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sPzgj","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T02:22:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T02:22:06Z","body":"Rendering meeting feedback:\r\n\r\nLooks good at first glance, exciting improvements in performance. To get this over the line we need:\r\n- reviews from knowledge holders (@lawnjelly @bruvzg if you have time that would be great)\r\n- testing, would be good to have a good test project for this so people can just download it and play around with it\r\n\r\nOn the Label2D improvements, agreed that this should be a follow up PR so we can move this forward.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3963566115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964565778","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3964565778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3964565778,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sTnkS","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T07:10:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T07:10:11Z","body":"> In case of label, batching will constantly break due to the nature of text rendering in most practical cases.\r\n\r\nEspecially problematic if using shadows, as it has to switch textures repeatedly. It sounds like what @bruvzg is doing is sorting so that both of those can be batched?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964565778/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965669755","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3965669755","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3965669755,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sX1F7","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T10:28:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T10:28:07Z","body":"> Especially problematic if using shadows, as it has to switch textures repeatedly. \r\n\r\nWithout looking in detail I'm not sure it was merged but I'm pretty sure I worked on modifying the 3.x code to draw shadows for a bunch of text at once, _then_ draw the text, so that there was no texture swap here with `MultiRect`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965669755/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965755997","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3965755997","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3965755997,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sYKJd","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T10:43:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T10:43:33Z","body":"> It sounds like what @bruvzg is doing is sorting so that both of those can be batched?\r\n\r\nShadows and outlines are always drawn for the whole line of text in separate steps, so it's not changing textures on every character draw. It's only an issue when the font uses multiple textures (pretty much always the case for complex CJK texts).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965755997/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968606810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3968606810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3968606810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sjCJa","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T19:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T19:03:55Z","body":"> Shadows and outlines are always drawn for the whole line of text in separate steps, so it's not changing textures on every character draw. It's only an issue when the font uses multiple textures (pretty much always the case for complex CJK texts).\r\n\r\npassivestar has a good test project, where it was switching for blocks of characters rather than the whole line. I'll see if I can dig it up.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968606810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968917803","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3968917803","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3968917803,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7skOEr","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T20:04:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T20:05:36Z","body":"> Shadows and outlines are always drawn for the whole line of text in separate steps, so it's not changing textures on every character draw.\r\n\r\nAlso batching Shadows/Outlines with regular character draws can't be done on this build yet - would require adding another Array parameter to the Multirect command so each Rect inside the Multirect could have the necessary distinct parameters, rather than configuring those at the level of the whole multirect.\r\n\r\n> In case of label, batching will constantly break due to the nature of text rendering in most practical cases. So not sure if it is worth doing explicitly, but might work a much better if it's done in conjunction with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116751 (and done automatically at the end of canvas_item_flush_presort, by replacing sequences of similar Rect commands with the MultiRect, or before frame drawing).\r\n\r\nThat does look like a great PR to do in conjunction! Another solution to this is to take a page from the TileMap implementation and use the helper class. Label communicates it's Draw Rect calls to Helper Class, Helper Class sorts commands and manages multiple internal Multirects, and at the end of drawing is when Helper Class actually flushes all of it's commands to the Command Stack.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968917803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968949615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-3968949615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":3968949615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7skV1v","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T20:09:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T20:11:55Z","body":">  Another solution to this is to take a page from the TileMap implementation and use the helper class. Label communicates it's Draw Rect calls to Helper Class, Helper Class sorts commands and manages multiple internal Multirects, and at the end of drawing is when Helper Class actually flushes all of it's commands to the Command Stack.\r\n\r\nThe original https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108369 was doing something similar, and that's what I'm trying to avoid with a new version, overcomplicated API with helper classes and unneeded communication (it might be OK for `TileMap`, but definite excessive for text).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3968949615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4242822753","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116613#issuecomment-4242822753","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116613","id":4242822753,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc785FZh","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T09:29:58Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T09:30:19Z","body":"Between re-basing and trying to implement FixedVector instead of Vector, a few things broke horribly in ways that were tricky to debug. \r\n\r\nI have rewound some of the changes and pushed a new build that is known good. Will tackle the Rebase and FixedVector again later this week. \r\n\r\nAlso note, this build has fully cut out any integration of Multirect command into Labels and the TextServer - this is to reduce conflicts and leave space for a more thoughtful integration in conjunction with BruvZG's work. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4242822753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]